    <statement><p>Suppose <m>t_0</m> is the <em>t</em>-coordinate of the point of intersection of the graphs below.  Complete the statement below in order to correctly describe what happens to <m>t_0</m> if the value of <m>r</m> (in the blue graph of <m>f(t)=a(1+r)^t</m> below) is increased, and all other quantities remain the same.</p>
<p>As <m>r</m> increases, does the value of <m>t_0</m> increase, decrease, or remain the same?
<var form="popup">
<li>
<p>increase</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Choose</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>decrease</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>remain the same</p>
</li>
</var></p>
